# The splash of .spun's GUI (BANK_screen/splash.c), against the test server.
# mame-splash.sh fills in @SPUN@ and @PORT@ and expands the @ lines
# (gui-test.py). .spun connects, then opens the GUI with the splash: S, P, U,
# N and the words STALE, PIXELS, UPDATES, NEXTS come up column by column and
# stop in line in the middle of the screen; then the list. @LAYER2 checks the
# splash's last picture, which stays in Layer 2 RAM after it. The run is at
# real speed.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
autostart .spun -p @PORT@
autostart PRINT "SPUNSPLASHDONE"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 24
noreset 7.5
mouse 2 move 128 128
# The pointer is hidden during the splash and a mouse move then does nothing;
# after it the pointer shows in the middle of the screen
mouse 9 move 30 30
@HIDDEN 9.5
@POINTER 9.5 160 128
@POINTER 12 160 128
@SHOWN 12
@LAYER2 14 splash splash
@ROWS 14 SPLIST 1
key 15 q
screen 23.9 SPUNSPLASHDONE
snap 8.6 8.8 9 9.2 9.4 9.6 9.8 10 10.2 10.34 14 23.9
